Data attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bill Commons ingests and republishes legislative data that originates from:

* Open States / Plural Policy (https://openstates.org) — bulk data and API
  access to U.S. state legislative bill, sponsor, vote, and session data.
  Open States is a project of Plural Policy. Open States' underlying data is
  aggregated from official state legislature websites and other public
  sources; see https://docs.openstates.org for details on source coverage
  and licensing.

* Official state and federal legislative websites and systems — the
  underlying bill text, actions, votes, and metadata are, in general,
  public-domain works of state and federal government bodies in the United
  States and are not subject to copyright protection under U.S. law
  (see 17 U.S.C. § 105 for federal works; most states apply an equivalent
  public-domain treatment to legislative and statutory text, though
  editorial annotations by third parties may not be).

* LegiScan (https://legiscan.com), where used as an optional (key-gated)
  supplementary source, per LegiScan's API terms of use.

Bill Commons does not claim copyright over the underlying legislative text,
actions, or votes obtained from these sources. Original code, schema design,
search/indexing logic, and presentation in this repository are licensed
under Apache-2.0 as described above.

